{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Hand-curated source-key -> behaviour IR mapping table, the behaviour counterpart of vocab/mappings.json. Edit by hand; nothing generates or infers it. A behaviour input plugin looks every fact it reads up here and applies the named converter; a fact with no row is reported in behaviour.unmapped.json (beside the IR directory) for a human to add a row. Source keys: `jsx:<tag>` (a host element), `jsx:<package>#<Export>` (a library component, after following local aliases and wrappers), `attr:<name>` (a JSX attribute on an element a `jsx:` row admits), `call:<package>#<path>` (a call whose callee resolves to a package export; `global#` is a browser global, `http#` an HTTP client method whose object argument spells a literal `url`), `zod:<method>` (one link of a zod chain). `when` matches a literal attribute value exactly. Rows only name libraries and the platform, never one site's own functions. The first matching row wins.",
  "converters": {
    "element": "the element's role for node matching (`role`, or `role_by_type` keyed by its literal `type`); `href_attr` names the attribute that carries its href",
    "passthrough": "no role of its own: the element is matched by what it renders (drop for matching, keep walking children)",
    "overlay_trigger": "a library trigger: tapping it does `does` on the nearest enclosing overlay of kind `overlay`",
    "overlay_close": "a library close control: tapping it closes the nearest enclosing overlay",
    "overlay_content": "everything under it renders inside the overlay (`in_overlay` true for node matching)",
    "overlay_root": "the overlay's root: `open` / `onOpenChange` bound to a useState pair make that state `controls` the overlay",
    "gesture": "an event-handler attribute: the trigger's gesture is `gesture`; the handler is walked for effects",
    "href": "a literal href: `/...` navigate, `#...` scroll_to, `<scheme>:` open_url",
    "new_tab": "x-web `new_tab: true` on the trigger",
    "submitter": "the element is a submit control of its enclosing form",
    "use_state": "`const [v, setV] = useState(init)`: state `<file>:<component>.<v>`; `setV(literal)` is a `set` effect",
    "navigator": "the hook returns a function; calling it with `{ to: literal }` is a `navigate` effect",
    "redirect": "`throw redirect({ to })` inside a guard: the guard's `go`",
    "file_route": "`createFileRoute(id)({ component, beforeLoad })`: a declared route at the id's URL (route groups `(x)` and pathless `_x` segments dropped); `component` is walked; `beforeLoad` is walked for guards; the route object's hooks are `call:route#<hook>` rows",
    "mutation": "`useMutation({ mutationFn, onSuccess, onError })`: calling a method in `methods` runs mutationFn; the awaited call in it gets on_success / on_failure from the callbacks, and what follows the await is success-path",
    "form": "`useForm({ resolver })`: calling a method in `methods` with a handler is a `validate` effect, then the handler's effects",
    "zod_resolver": "`zodResolver(schema)`: the zod object schema the form validates against",
    "show": "a `show` effect on `surface` with `tone`; the first literal string argument is the `title`",
    "storage": "x-web storage read/write (`op`) of the literal key in the first argument",
    "http_operation": "an HTTP operation: `method` from the row, `url` from the literal `url` property of the object argument",
    "zod_rule": "one validation rule `rule`; the first numeric/string argument is `value`, a `{ message }` argument is `message`",
    "drop": "known, carries no behaviour fact; never reported",
    "wrapper": "A component wrapper call (forwardRef, memo): the component is the function passed as the first argument.",
    "constraint": "HTML constraint validation on a host input / textarea / select: one rule `rule` for the field named by its literal `name`; `value: true` takes the attribute's literal as the rule's value; the message is the browser's, so `null`"
  },
